{"created": "2018-06-11T12:28:14.358619+00:00", "modified": "2024-08-02T14:09:46.809440+00:00", "id": 1286904, "conceptrecid": "1286903", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.1286904", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.1286903", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1286904", "metadata": {"title": "Latest Results from the CUORE Experiment", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.1286904", "publication_date": "2018-06-06", "description": "<p>The Cryogenic Underground Observatory for Rare Events (CUORE) is the first bolometric experiment searching for neutrinoless double beta decay (0&nu;&beta;&beta;) that has been able to reach the one-ton scale. The detector consists of an array of 988 TeO2 crystals arranged in a compact cylindrical structure of 19 towers. The construction of the experiment was completed in August 2016 with the installation of all towers in the cryostat. Following a cooldown, diagnostic, and optimization campaign, routine data-taking began in spring 2017. After the first two months of data taking, CUORE collected a total TeO2 exposure of 86.3 kg&middot;yr with an average energy resolution of 7.7 keV FWHM and a background in the region of interest of 0.014 counts/(keV&middot;kg&middot;yr). With this dataset, CUORE placed a lower limit on the 130Te 0&nu;&beta;&beta; half-life of &gt; 1.3 &times; 10<sup>25</sup> yr (90% C.L.). In this talk, we report on the latest evaluation of the CUORE background budget, and using this same 86.3 kg&middot;yr dataset, we present the most precise measurement of the 130Te 0&nu;&beta;&beta; half-life to date.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Ouellet, Jonathan", "affiliation": "MIT"}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.10342", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "scheme": "url"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Presentation", "type": "presentation"}, "meeting": {"title": "XXVIII International Conference on Neutrino Physics and Astrophysics", "acronym": "Neutrino 2018", "dates": "4-9 June 2018", "place": "Heidelberg, Germany", "url": "https://www.mpi-hd.mpg.de/nu2018/", "session": "Double Beta Decay", "session_part": "2"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "communities": [{"id": "neutrino2018"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "1286903"}}]}}, "title": "Latest Results from the CUORE Experiment", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/1286904", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/1286904", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/1286904?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1286904", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1286904", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.1286904", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/1286904/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/1286903", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/1286903", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1286903", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.1286903", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:1286904/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:1286904/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/1286904/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/1286904/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:1286904:CUORE_Neutrino2018_ForWebpage_Ouellet.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:1286904:CUORE_Neutrino2018_ForWebpage_Ouellet.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:1286904:CUORE_Neutrino2018_ForWebpage_Ouellet.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:1286904:CUORE_Neutrino2018_ForWebpage_Ouellet.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:1286904:CUORE_Neutrino2018_ForWebpage_Ouellet.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:1286904:CUORE_Neutrino2018_ForWebpage_O